  "labelNotes": "Supply rows in Recommended Operating Conditions (p7): VCC 2-6 V (HC types) and 4.5-5.5 V (HCT types), VCC-VEE 2-10 V, VEE 0 (MIN column) to -6 (MAX column). The VCC-VEE MIN of 2 V duplicates the HC VCC MIN tuple (2 V MIN, no conditions) so it is one label. The 'TA = full package temperature range' condition is not numeric and is omitted. The HC/HCT VCC values sit on lines with no parameter text, so their citations are the value-line text itself (spans cells). Abs max: VEE row prints 0.5 under MIN and -7 under MAX; labelled -7 as ABS_MAX because it is the MAX column (doubtful: it is a negative-rail rating). VCC-VEE 10.5 V treated as a supply-voltage row. The logic control input pin voltage (VSEL/VEN) prints 30 V as its MAX; labelled as printed even though it looks unusual. ICC 50 mA in Abs Max is a DC current limit, not a supply current, and IIK/IOK are clamp currents, so quiescent and leakage are ABSENT on pages 6-8 (p8 only holds VIH/VIL). RL = 100 ohm is a load, not a pull-up."
